@1.5
May 2011...

@+0.5
MMD development has ended

@+0.5
For that itself, we'd like to send it off with respect

@+0.5
However, MMD left behind an unrealized feature

@+0.5
"That feature" has now been revived thanks to the power of MME

@+0.5
I'd like to name "it"

:size 26
:fade 0.5

@+1.2
MikuMikuTelop

:timebase 54

:valign_bottom

:fade 0.5
:size 12
:pos_y -90
:edge 12
:autotime 0.28

:set miku

@0
Hello everyone

@+1
You may have already noticed

@+1
This video does not use any external editing software at all

@+1
Without any exceptions — in other words

@+1
Even this subtitle was rendered in MMD

@+1.5
Well then, let me introduce it

@+1
This is MikuMikuTelop itself

:autotime 0.24

@+2
The design is so simple it's almost disappointing...

@+1
But this tool works by reading subtitle description files from outside
to generate subtitle effects

@+1
And for describing subtitles, it uses
a simple subtitle description language called "MMTScript"

@+1
But don't worry, you don't need to be too nervous

:autotime 0.2

@+1
The simplest MMTScript just adds
an @ symbol and display time before the text

:autotime 0.24

:align_left

@+1
For example,

@@164
Subtitle test

If you write it like this...

//Reset format
:get default
:timebase 0

@164
Subtitle test

//Restore format
:get miku

:autotime 0.23

@+-2
It will be displayed for 164 seconds like this.

@+30F
Besides this, it has many other features...

@+1
That will be introduced in the next video.

@+1,8
That's all for my introduction
Well then, until we meet again...

@+1,5
Goodbye


